From 79b65bdb9b15c07ee5de7c25846ccb740b008e38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nanegate <67761222+nanegate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:13:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ENH: ODE: add sparse LU and autonomous derivative reuse to
 seulex

- factorise (1/dx)I - J with a minimum-degree symbolic/numeric sparse
  LU solver (seulexSparseLU) when the symbolic factorisation requires
  fewer than half the multiply-adds of dense LU
- skip leading zero blocks during sparse forward substitution and fall
  back to dense LU with partial pivoting on small pivots
- absorb new non-zero Jacobian entries that land in existing fill-in
  positions without rebuilding the symbolic factorisation
- add optional autonomous switch (default: false) to share the initial
  step derivative f(y0) across extrapolation columns and reuse the
  divergence-test derivative evaluation on the subsequent substep
- add optional sparse switch (default: true) and register seulexFast
  as a runtime selection alias for backward compatibility
